WEBVTT

00:14.139 --> 00:17.183
What I really loved the most...

00:23.690 --> 00:25.692
was watching Dad's stories from here.

00:28.737 --> 00:30.905
FIRST STORY
THAT DAY

00:36.911 --> 00:42.792
So then the landlord came over,
and said, "Look, I'm taking your toolbox."

00:42.876 --> 00:48.089
I'm thinking, "Oh, the landlord's
gonna work as a carpenter?"

00:48.173 --> 00:50.425
So I say, "Here you go!"
and I lent it to him.

00:50.508 --> 00:52.093
As if he could do carpentry at his...

00:52.177 --> 00:53.011
SHINTA ARAKAWA

00:53.094 --> 00:54.471
He must be senile.

00:54.554 --> 00:56.306
No, you're the senile one!

00:56.890 --> 00:59.768
You... Wait, are you telling me that...

01:01.436 --> 01:03.938
Stiff! You sound so stiff, Shin-chan!

01:04.522 --> 01:06.357
I do?

01:06.441 --> 01:08.735
That's right.
Too much pressure on yourself.

01:08.818 --> 01:11.279
Oh. You think so?

01:12.697 --> 01:14.157
You've got that test coming up,

01:14.240 --> 01:16.117
and your little girl is getting bigger.

01:16.201 --> 01:19.454
So I don't blame you for tensing up, but...

01:24.501 --> 01:28.087
You need to be more...
smooth as silk, then boom!

01:28.171 --> 01:29.506
Give it your all, okay?

01:29.589 --> 01:30.882
Thank you very much.

01:34.427 --> 01:36.554
You think highly of him, don't you?

01:36.638 --> 01:40.850
If you ask me, he's pretty bland,
and his style doesn't really do it for me.

01:40.934 --> 01:43.520
Well, I admit he was rather sub-par today.

01:43.603 --> 01:44.562
Then why?

01:47.148 --> 01:51.736
Well, I once saw him
deliver a brilliant performance.

01:54.072 --> 01:58.493
He's not the kind of man who should
be languishing in a place like this.

02:05.333 --> 02:06.334
MITSUE ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

02:06.417 --> 02:07.627
It's Akane's...

02:07.710 --> 02:09.629
MITSUE ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

02:13.675 --> 02:16.761
Hey! How can you say that?

02:16.845 --> 02:20.098
- How dare you...
- Gimme a break. I just told you...

02:20.181 --> 02:22.308
Don't talk to me like that!

02:22.392 --> 02:23.268
Oh, can't you see

02:23.351 --> 02:24.561
- how hard my son's crying?
- Mrs. Ozaki,

02:24.644 --> 02:27.355
- please, your voice...
- Don't you feel sorry for him?

02:27.438 --> 02:28.982
I can't believe children these days.

02:29.065 --> 02:31.234
You haven't heard a word I've said.

02:33.153 --> 02:36.614
Fine. Then I'll show you, so please watch.

02:37.323 --> 02:38.449
Show us?

02:40.285 --> 02:44.122
So, it all started during
fifth period, in Japanese class.

02:44.205 --> 02:49.294
We were reading aloud our essays on
"The Person I Respect," one by one.

02:49.377 --> 02:50.962
The Person I Respect.

02:51.045 --> 02:52.922
Grade 5, Class 3. Akane Osaki.

02:53.006 --> 02:55.592
The person I respect is my dad.

02:55.675 --> 02:59.053
Dad is a Rakugoka, and he tells
the funniest stories ever.

03:00.179 --> 03:02.640
Respect? Huh, that's crazy.

03:02.724 --> 03:05.810
I heard from my mom, you know.
She says your dad's a kept man.

03:05.894 --> 03:07.520
And you respect him?

03:07.604 --> 03:08.938
Kept man? What's that?

03:09.939 --> 03:12.025
You don't even know what that is?

03:12.108 --> 03:13.985
- It's a deadbeat dad...
- Oh, crap!

03:14.068 --> 03:15.862
...who doesn't even work, got that?

03:15.945 --> 03:17.739
Amazing.

03:18.406 --> 03:21.492
I mean, that's exactly how it happened.

03:21.576 --> 03:24.245
But that doesn't mean
she can make him cry!

03:24.871 --> 03:29.751
You've been making him the victim,
but he's the one who started it.

03:29.834 --> 03:32.211
Don't give me that crap, you demented ha--

03:32.295 --> 03:34.339
Knock it off.

03:34.422 --> 03:35.840
Dad! Wait, why...

03:35.924 --> 03:38.635
Sorry, Mr. Yanagiya.

03:38.718 --> 03:41.262
Akane's always getting into trouble.

03:41.346 --> 03:44.432
My apologies to you, too.

03:45.391 --> 03:47.644
Dad! These jerks are...

03:47.727 --> 03:49.479
These jerks?

03:50.772 --> 03:54.067
Whatever the reason may be,
it's wrong to use abusive language.

03:54.692 --> 03:56.402
I know you understand, right, Akane?

03:56.486 --> 03:59.280
It certainly helps that you're
a reasonable man.

03:59.364 --> 04:02.659
- That child is truly--
- Mr. Yanagiya told me what happened.

04:02.742 --> 04:06.371
Both mother and son
were talking about me in a way.

04:07.413 --> 04:11.292
We should both try to live up
to our kids' expectations, yes?

04:13.336 --> 04:14.170
COUNSELING ROOM

04:14.254 --> 04:17.465
All right, then. Let's get going, Akane.

04:21.386 --> 04:23.888
- Go get your things, okay?
- Okay!

04:43.074 --> 04:45.326
Yeah, this is tasty.

04:46.035 --> 04:48.579
Eat up, Akane. Or it'll melt.

04:51.499 --> 04:52.792
I'm sorry.

04:54.460 --> 04:57.964
I only yelled back because I wanted
to tell him how great you are.

04:59.048 --> 05:02.343
But I think I just
made you feel bad instead.

05:08.433 --> 05:09.976
You dummy.

05:10.059 --> 05:13.730
You're too young
to be looking out for my feelings.

05:17.191 --> 05:20.111
Rakugoka are divided into three levels.

05:20.194 --> 05:24.699
The lowest is Zenza, then Futatsume,
and finally Shin'uchi.

05:24.782 --> 05:26.743
You're a Futatsume, right, Dad?

05:26.826 --> 05:28.244
I'm impressed you remembered.

05:32.040 --> 05:35.460
There's going to be a test
for promotion to Shin'uchi.

05:36.586 --> 05:38.963
And if I pass,
I'll get to become a Shin'uchi.

05:40.465 --> 05:42.717
As a Shin'uchi, I can rake in some...

05:43.801 --> 05:45.636
I'll earn lots of money.

05:47.930 --> 05:50.349
And then no one will ever say
a word against me!

05:52.435 --> 05:55.063
So don't worry about me like that.

05:55.146 --> 05:56.814
All you need to do is stick to your guns!

05:58.608 --> 06:00.860
All right, I'm gonna rehearse.

06:00.943 --> 06:02.653
You go do your homework, Akane!

06:02.737 --> 06:04.697
- Okay!
- Good.

06:12.497 --> 06:13.915
Yeah, right?

06:19.253 --> 06:22.215
I'm going to become a Shin'uchi.
I have to.

06:23.216 --> 06:24.050
Or else...

06:33.392 --> 06:37.271
All right. Why don't I start
by reviewing today's material?

06:38.147 --> 06:41.776
Hey, Yota! Yotaro! Yota!

06:45.113 --> 06:46.364
Oh, geez.

06:46.447 --> 06:49.367
Must be the curry udon I had for lunch.

06:49.867 --> 06:54.539
Still, how insanely pissed
is Mrs. Ozaki? Gross.

06:55.623 --> 07:00.503
Ugh, that Akane and Tohru...
They've done it again.

07:01.796 --> 07:03.464
I'm home!

07:04.132 --> 07:06.968
Oh, darn, not again! Curry twice in a day.

07:07.552 --> 07:11.347
Really now, how curry-crazed are we?

07:11.431 --> 07:13.057
Oh well, can't be helped.

07:13.141 --> 07:15.351
Oh, uh... uh... Yota, hey you.

07:15.435 --> 07:17.437
You went in from there?

07:17.520 --> 07:20.565
Y-You, come on, you.
Don't try to come in from the front, okay?

07:20.648 --> 07:22.442
Go in from the back, okay?

07:22.525 --> 07:24.193
You sit tight now. Yeah.

07:26.571 --> 07:27.488
I can see.

07:27.572 --> 07:30.074
Uh, excuse me! Hello!

07:30.158 --> 07:32.827
There's no one in the room but Dad.

07:32.910 --> 07:36.539
And yet... inside the room...

07:36.622 --> 07:37.999
There are three people.

07:38.082 --> 07:39.876
Every time he turns his body,

07:39.959 --> 07:42.837
his face, manner of speaking,
and his voice all change on a dime.

07:42.920 --> 07:46.007
A spiteful person. An ill-tempered person.
A nonchalant person.

07:46.090 --> 07:47.967
All kinds of people appear.

07:48.050 --> 07:51.345
So amazing! It's like magic.

07:56.476 --> 07:58.102
No thanks, damn it!

07:58.186 --> 07:59.604
How does he do it?

07:59.687 --> 08:03.316
O-Old woman! The boss is here!

08:03.399 --> 08:06.569
Hey, there. Your mother is home!

08:10.573 --> 08:12.950
Really, I'm surrounded by Rakugo crazies.

08:17.663 --> 08:19.373
Oh, well, what can you do?

08:20.124 --> 08:21.209
It is next week, after all.

08:26.422 --> 08:28.257
Thank you for this meal!

08:31.969 --> 08:32.887
Yummy!

08:33.763 --> 08:37.099
Yeah. It's good!
This turned out well, huh?

08:41.854 --> 08:43.689
Good night!

08:47.443 --> 08:48.528
Hey!

08:48.611 --> 08:50.196
Wake up, Tohru!

08:51.447 --> 08:53.115
Come on! Hey!

08:53.199 --> 08:55.034
Weren't you going to rehearse some more?

08:55.117 --> 08:56.118
Or go to bed?

08:57.745 --> 09:00.081
- Rehearse.
- Then get to it!

09:00.164 --> 09:03.793
It's late. I'll be going to bed, okay?

09:05.336 --> 09:09.799
By the way, Tohru,
did you read Akane's essay?

09:09.882 --> 09:11.717
Huh? No.

09:19.976 --> 09:22.645
THE PERSON I RESPECT

09:45.710 --> 09:47.378
SAIWAI HALL
TODAY'S EVENT

09:47.461 --> 09:49.171
SAIWAI HALL
ARAKAWA SCHOOL

09:49.255 --> 09:51.799
This way to reception!

09:55.886 --> 09:56.762
ARAKAWA SCHOOL
SHIN'UCHI PROMOTION TEST

09:56.846 --> 09:59.265
Hey, it's Dad!
It's bigger than the one at home!

09:59.348 --> 10:00.766
What, you think so?

10:00.850 --> 10:02.059
It looks the same to me.

10:02.143 --> 10:04.270
Hey, someone's full of energy!

10:04.353 --> 10:05.187
SHIGUMA ARAKAWA

10:05.271 --> 10:06.606
Master Shiguma!

10:06.689 --> 10:08.733
Long time no see, Masaki.

10:09.734 --> 10:10.985
It's been a long time.

10:11.068 --> 10:13.029
Thank you for taking care of my husband.

10:13.112 --> 10:15.239
No, no, I haven't done a thing.

10:15.323 --> 10:18.451
Still, time certainly goes by fast.

10:18.534 --> 10:20.369
Hey, Master, where's Dad?

10:20.453 --> 10:21.329
Dummy!

10:22.997 --> 10:24.874
Well, you know.

10:24.957 --> 10:27.627
You should leave him be right now.

10:30.004 --> 10:33.257
The Arakawa School
Shin'uchi Promotion Test.

10:34.008 --> 10:37.386
The performances are evaluated
by the audience and the jury.

10:37.470 --> 10:38.596
After adding up all the scores,

10:38.679 --> 10:43.017
only those whose skills have been
recognized can be promoted to Shin'uchi.

10:43.100 --> 10:46.062
This year, the president of the jury will
be my master's elder fellow apprentice...

10:46.145 --> 10:47.021
Thank you for taking the time!

10:47.104 --> 10:49.940
...and the most acclaimed of his day.

10:53.736 --> 10:55.029
Issho Arakawa!

10:57.531 --> 11:00.576
S-So what if he is?

11:00.660 --> 11:04.288
Just how hard have I worked for this day?

11:04.372 --> 11:07.750
Just carry on as always,
and believe in your own art.

11:08.459 --> 11:09.585
But...

11:10.378 --> 11:12.213
If I do mess up...

11:13.756 --> 11:14.757
No!

11:15.758 --> 11:17.301
What am I, an idiot?

11:17.385 --> 11:19.345
I can't surrender to my emotions!

11:20.554 --> 11:22.640
I just have to do it! For me...

11:22.723 --> 11:24.809
there's no other option!

11:25.643 --> 11:27.395
ARAKAWA SCHOOL
SHIN'UCHI PROMOTION TEST

11:27.478 --> 11:30.856
Okay, so let's get started.

11:30.940 --> 11:35.694
We will now begin the Arakawa School
Shin'uchi Promotion Test!

11:36.445 --> 11:40.157
Our first performer is... this man!

12:02.805 --> 12:08.185
I happen to be the first one up,
and my name is Shinta Arakawa.

12:10.312 --> 12:12.231
This is nothing like the typical events.

12:12.314 --> 12:13.941
The air is heavy and cold.

12:16.444 --> 12:20.072
Most of all, the audience's eyes
are appraising me.

12:21.031 --> 12:23.784
Well, I do appreciate you all

12:23.868 --> 12:28.247
coming to this tasteless test
on such a glorious day.

12:28.831 --> 12:30.916
- No, seriously.
- This is bad.

12:31.000 --> 12:32.293
Or not?

12:32.376 --> 12:34.545
With one vote from you,
my life will change.

12:34.628 --> 12:36.130
You idiot, what are you thinking?

12:36.213 --> 12:38.716
I kind of sound like a politician!

12:38.799 --> 12:39.884
In which case, I wish...

12:39.967 --> 12:41.886
For now, focus on your prologue!

12:47.475 --> 12:50.311
W-Well, since I am a Rakugoka...

12:50.394 --> 12:53.105
Not good. The tempo's too fast.

12:53.189 --> 12:55.316
And that's another way
of being like a politician!

12:55.399 --> 12:57.318
I'm not getting any laughs.
Was I too greedy?

12:57.401 --> 12:59.320
Please give me your precious vote!

12:59.403 --> 13:01.280
What should I do? At this rate...

13:01.363 --> 13:02.239
This...

13:08.621 --> 13:09.788
That voice...

13:14.668 --> 13:17.421
What? Akane is mimicking me?

13:17.505 --> 13:18.339
That's right.

13:18.422 --> 13:22.593
I'm no expert,
but she's actually really good.

13:22.676 --> 13:24.762
She might have
a better feel for it than you.

13:24.845 --> 13:26.555
Well, then I'm in trouble.

13:26.639 --> 13:29.850
If that's your attitude,
then just become a Shin'uchi already!

13:29.934 --> 13:31.393
Don't make it sound so easy!

13:31.477 --> 13:34.313
But I will. Because it's for Akane's sake!

13:34.396 --> 13:35.272
Akane's sake?

13:35.356 --> 13:37.107
I don't believe you.

13:37.191 --> 13:38.984
Akane's a daddy's girl, you know.

13:39.068 --> 13:42.112
Of course she wants to brag about you.

13:43.030 --> 13:46.325
You can whimper
all you want in front of me,

13:48.160 --> 13:52.623
but at least be a cool father
in front of Akane, okay?

13:58.254 --> 14:00.214
There's quite a chill in the air.

14:01.048 --> 14:03.133
- But the cold isn't all bad.
- What's this?

14:03.217 --> 14:06.554
How great does heated up sake
taste on a cold day?

14:06.637 --> 14:10.307
You can't stop yourself from
reaching for another, and another.

14:11.267 --> 14:15.229
Before you know it, you're in a dreamy
state, gulping down until you mess up...

14:15.312 --> 14:16.897
The atmosphere changed.

14:16.981 --> 14:19.316
...which happens all too often.

14:20.985 --> 14:22.194
Wake up, dear!

14:22.278 --> 14:25.781
Dear! Come on, wake up! Dear!

14:25.865 --> 14:27.700
What the heck? Huh?

14:28.367 --> 14:30.452
Don't wake me up
in that harsh way. What is it?

14:30.536 --> 14:32.162
Don't give me that!

14:32.246 --> 14:35.749
He finished his prologue
and went into the story?

14:36.500 --> 14:37.626
SHINTA ARAKAWA

14:37.710 --> 14:39.545
SHIBAHAMA

14:42.381 --> 14:44.633
Katsugoro is a skilled fishmonger,

14:44.717 --> 14:47.845
but he drinks like a fish
and is drowning in debt.

14:47.928 --> 14:50.806
After he finds a wallet
on the beach of Shiba,

14:50.890 --> 14:53.559
he regains his pride as a merchant.

14:53.642 --> 14:56.562
It's a heart-warming Ninjo-banashi.

14:58.480 --> 15:00.065
I'm counting on you.

15:00.149 --> 15:02.568
Right! Be careful out there, okay?

15:03.694 --> 15:07.239
Now, after seeing her husband off,
the wife breathed a sigh of relief because

15:07.323 --> 15:11.660
for the first time in a while,
he was heading to work and to do business.

15:11.744 --> 15:14.288
And her eyelids grew heavy,

15:14.371 --> 15:17.041
and just as she started
nodding off, nodding off...

15:17.124 --> 15:19.585
Hey! Honey!

15:19.668 --> 15:21.712
It's me! Open up! Honey!

15:22.296 --> 15:23.339
Yes, yes, of course!

15:23.422 --> 15:24.924
Oh, hold on a second.

15:25.007 --> 15:25.925
I'm coming...

15:28.761 --> 15:29.803
What's the matter?

15:29.887 --> 15:32.014
Never mind! Never mind that.
Close the door, honey!

15:32.097 --> 15:33.432
I said close the door!

15:37.895 --> 15:41.982
So he deleted the scene where Katsugoro
goes to the beach of Shiba.

15:42.066 --> 15:44.944
I mean, that's totally fine.

15:45.527 --> 15:47.071
So long as the main storyline fits,

15:47.154 --> 15:50.532
you can change everything from
the characters' settings to the punchline.

15:50.616 --> 15:52.660
That's one way to innovate.

15:53.327 --> 15:54.828
That said, describing the sight

15:55.829 --> 16:01.585
of the beach of Shiba when Katsugoro
stops by on his way to the shore...

16:01.669 --> 16:04.129
That's the appeal of Shibahama.

16:05.214 --> 16:09.343
But cutting out the only scene
of the beach of Shiba in Shibahama...

16:09.426 --> 16:12.805
- It's like an empty bean-paste bun.
- Look how annoyed he is.

16:12.888 --> 16:15.349
After all, this is the kind of approach
that Zenshou Ani-san loathes.

16:16.558 --> 16:18.310
Well, I do get it, though.

16:18.394 --> 16:21.563
It doesn't change the fact that he
threw out a highlight of the story.

16:21.647 --> 16:23.357
Hey, j-just a second there, honey.

16:23.440 --> 16:27.361
Still, rather than talking about
the scenery...

16:27.987 --> 16:31.490
You haven't gone anywhere, can't you see?

16:31.573 --> 16:33.075
The beach of Shiba?

16:33.158 --> 16:36.245
He chose to talk about the people.

16:36.328 --> 16:39.248
I woke you up this morning.
And I didn't go to Shiba.

16:39.331 --> 16:42.376
Shinta's strength is his acting prowess.

16:42.459 --> 16:44.003
By deliberately throwing out a key scene,

16:44.086 --> 16:47.631
and pushing his descriptions
of the characters onto them,

16:47.715 --> 16:50.050
he draws the audience into the story.

16:50.134 --> 16:52.803
On this stage, no less.

16:53.846 --> 16:57.558
Wait, this wife is similar to...

16:57.641 --> 16:59.768
- It's you, Mom.
- What?

17:01.186 --> 17:04.565
Dad... He's acting out you, Mom!

17:05.065 --> 17:08.318
Akane, Masaki, are you watching this?

17:10.237 --> 17:12.322
Since I started training under my master,

17:12.406 --> 17:14.908
and threw myself into Rakugo,
it's been 13 years.

17:16.201 --> 17:19.038
I was so unsuccessful, it was scary.

17:20.622 --> 17:22.624
I wasn't earning a decent living, either.

17:26.879 --> 17:31.091
Even so, Masaki never told me
to quit Rakugo.

17:32.301 --> 17:33.218
And Akane...

17:33.802 --> 17:35.471
"The Person I Respect."

17:35.554 --> 17:38.098
Grade 5, Class 3. Akane Osaki.

17:38.766 --> 17:42.352
The person I respect more than anyone
else in the world is my dad.

17:42.853 --> 17:46.523
Dad is a Rakugoka,
and he's really great at telling stories.

17:46.607 --> 17:49.276
He makes me laugh every single day.

17:49.777 --> 17:53.030
It's Dad's dream to become a Shin'uchi.

17:53.530 --> 17:56.658
And it's also my dream
for Dad to become a Shin'uchi.

17:57.618 --> 18:00.245
I love my dad so much.

18:00.329 --> 18:04.458
Akane still loved me through it all.

18:07.086 --> 18:08.796
I want to live up to that love.

18:09.755 --> 18:12.716
As a father. As a Rakugoka.

18:13.217 --> 18:17.596
All of the skills I've nurtured until now,
along with my life, and everything...

18:18.263 --> 18:20.307
I'll gather it all in.

18:21.892 --> 18:25.521
And today,
I'm going to become a Shin'uchi!

18:29.149 --> 18:30.150
No, I'll pass.

18:31.026 --> 18:32.736
I don't want it
to turn into another dream.

18:41.078 --> 18:42.663
Awesome!

18:43.664 --> 18:46.375
Dad... You're so cool!

18:48.127 --> 18:49.628
SAIWAI HALL

18:49.711 --> 18:53.173
Sorry to keep you waiting for so long!

18:53.257 --> 18:55.801
Apparently, we have all the results now.

18:55.884 --> 18:58.345
It's all good, right? It's all good!

18:58.428 --> 18:59.263
Be quiet.

19:00.055 --> 19:02.808
The results will be announced by Arakawa...

19:02.891 --> 19:05.060
M-Master Issho! If you please...

19:07.604 --> 19:09.314
Ah, it's on, then?

19:10.149 --> 19:12.526
I'd like to thank you all

19:12.609 --> 19:18.949
for attending this Arakawa School
Shin'uchi Promotion Test.

19:19.533 --> 19:24.496
For the first time in a while, I got
a look at the youngsters' material.

19:24.580 --> 19:26.790
Really, I was shocked.

19:26.874 --> 19:30.294
Well, it won't do any good
to drag this on,

19:30.377 --> 19:32.754
so let me announce the results.

19:32.838 --> 19:37.968
Everyone who took part
in today's test is hereby expelled.

19:41.972 --> 19:43.515
B-But Master, surely you're joking.

19:43.599 --> 19:48.604
These disgraces to my school
put on utterly pitiful performances.

19:48.687 --> 19:50.272
For that I apologize.

19:56.945 --> 19:59.239
All right, so there you have it.

19:59.323 --> 20:00.157
That's all.

20:00.240 --> 20:03.327
Oh! W-Wait, Master!

20:03.410 --> 20:04.953
Hey, what's going on?

20:05.037 --> 20:06.163
What does expelled mean?

20:06.246 --> 20:07.539
Hey, Mom!

20:07.623 --> 20:09.333
Did you hear me, Mom?

20:09.416 --> 20:10.959
Hey, Mom!

20:11.043 --> 20:12.252
Tohru.

20:15.047 --> 20:17.007
SAIWAI HALL

20:17.090 --> 20:17.883
SAIWAI HALL TODAY'S EVENT

20:17.966 --> 20:20.302
Listen, what's the meaning of this?

20:20.385 --> 20:21.345
Expelled?

20:21.428 --> 20:23.555
Shinta's my apprentice!

20:24.556 --> 20:29.603
Later, everyone who took the test
that day was officially expelled.

20:29.686 --> 20:31.647
You can't just expel
my apprentice without--

20:31.730 --> 20:34.483
What an incompetent apprentice you had.

20:35.817 --> 20:38.695
The reason for expelling them
was never revealed.

20:40.530 --> 20:44.243
You can't call that thing Shibahama.

20:48.288 --> 20:50.916
What? You mean it's for real?

20:51.416 --> 20:52.709
Shinta...

20:52.793 --> 20:54.753
Shinta Ani-san, what's going on here?

20:54.836 --> 20:55.921
It's just a joke, right?

20:56.004 --> 20:58.924
It has to be. Come on, Shinta Ani-san!

21:02.928 --> 21:03.971
That day...

21:04.846 --> 21:07.474
the Rakugoka, Shinta Arakawa, died.

21:17.776 --> 21:20.153
RYOKUGYOKU HIGH SCHOOL
EVENT CALENDAR

21:22.281 --> 21:23.115
That day...

21:24.950 --> 21:27.786
the Rakugoka, Shinta Arakawa, died.

21:30.497 --> 21:31.331
But...

21:35.419 --> 21:36.878
It's not over.

21:48.598 --> 21:49.599
In fact...

21:51.476 --> 21:53.520
That was the day it started.

21:59.943 --> 22:01.862
My story!

23:36.164 --> 23:37.916
NEXT EPISODE
FIRST PERFORMANCE

23:38.792 --> 23:40.293
Akane Small Talk!

23:44.381 --> 23:46.258
Dad! Okay, I have a question!

23:46.341 --> 23:48.093
Sure, what is it?

23:48.176 --> 23:50.887
Why is Rakugo called Rakugo?

23:50.971 --> 23:53.849
Right, because...
You know how Rakugo has a "sage"

23:53.932 --> 23:55.767
or in other words, an "ochi"?

23:55.851 --> 23:58.311
It used to be called "Otoshi-banashi."

23:58.395 --> 24:01.273
That got shortened
to "Rakugo", or so they say.

24:01.356 --> 24:02.566
Oh, really?

24:02.649 --> 24:04.568
Okay, I have another question!

24:04.651 --> 24:08.613
Don't your legs get tingly
from sitting for so long?

24:08.697 --> 24:11.241
Well, they'd get tingly
if all I was doing was sitting,

24:11.324 --> 24:14.202
but when you perform Rakugo, you actually
move a lot while you're talking.

24:14.286 --> 24:17.205
So you don't end up getting too tingly
that you can't stand up.

24:17.289 --> 24:18.498
I see.

24:18.582 --> 24:19.666
Oh, question!

24:19.749 --> 24:21.293
Yes, Ms. Akane?

24:21.376 --> 24:23.670
Why do you take off your haori
in the middle?

24:23.753 --> 24:24.838
If you're going to take it off right away,

24:24.921 --> 24:26.882
you might as well
not wear it from the start.

24:26.965 --> 24:31.052
It's better to be properly dressed
when you show up before an audience.

24:31.136 --> 24:34.556
So you take it off when you're ready
to get to the heart of the story.

24:34.639 --> 24:38.351
Not that there are any hard-and-fast rules
about when you're supposed to remove it.

24:38.435 --> 24:41.521
Oh? I'd like to give that a try myself!

24:41.605 --> 24:43.440
I'd start out wearing tons of them,

24:43.523 --> 24:45.734
and then I'd go on shedding
one haori after another!

24:47.444 --> 24:49.321
Sounds like a hassle
to tidy up afterwards.
